---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="2026 Website & Lead Gen Guide for Malaysian SMEs — HaikaiTech"
  description=""
  canonical="https://haikaitech.my/guide-content/"
  noindex
>
  <style is:global>
    /* Print-focused authoring page — the source for the guide PDF. */
    .guide-page {
      font-family: Inter, Arial, sans-serif;
      color: #1e293b;
      background: #fff;
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 40px 48px;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }
    .guide-page h1 { font-size: 32px; line-height: 1.2; color: #0f172a; margin: 0 0 8px; }
    .guide-page h2 { font-size: 20px; color: #1d4ed8; margin: 36px 0 8px; }
    .guide-page h3 { font-size: 16px; color: #0f172a; margin: 24px 0 6px; }
    .guide-page p { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 12px; color: #334155; }
    .guide-page ul, .guide-page ol { font-size: 14px; color: #334155; margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 22px; }
    .guide-page li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
    .guide-page .sub { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #64748b; }
    .guide-page .lead { font-size: 16px; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 16px; }
    .guide-page .box { background: #f1f5f9; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; margin: 16px 0; }
    .guide-page .box h3 { margin-top: 0; }
    .guide-page .tag { display: inline-block; background: #059669; color: #fff; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; border-radius: 999px; padding: 3px 10px; vertical-align: middle; }
    .guide-page .quote { border-left: 3px solid #1d4ed8; padding: 4px 0 4px 14px; font-style: italic; color: #475569; margin: 12px 0; }
    .guide-page .script { background: #0f172a; color: #e2e8f0; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 14px; font-size: 13px; margin: 8px 0; }
    .guide-page .script strong { color: #34d399; }
    .guide-page .two-col { display: flex; gap: 24px; }
    .guide-page .fact { font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 22px; color: #1d4ed8; }
    .guide-page .cta { text-align: center; margin-top: 32px; padding: 20px; background: #0f172a; color: #fff; border-radius: 12px; }
    .guide-page .cta a { color: #34d399; font-weight: 700; }
    .guide-page .page-break { page-break-before: always; }

    @media print {
      @page { margin: 16mm; }
      body { background: #fff; }
      .guide-page { box-shadow: none; padding: 0; }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="guide-page">
    <p class="sub">HaikaiTech Solutions · Malaysia</p>
    <h1>2026 Website &amp; Lead Gen Guide for Malaysian SMEs</h1>
    <p class="sub">How much things really cost, and how to get leads from your site</p>

    <p class="lead">
      This short guide gives you the pricing reality for websites, web apps and dashboards in Malaysia, a clear look
      at how fixed-price work (instead of hourly surprises), and practical lead-gen steps — including WhatsApp reply
      scripts you can copy-paste today.
    </p>

    <div class="box">
      <h3>What's inside</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>What a Malaysian SME website actually costs</li>
        <li>The fixed-price model (why it's safer for you)</li>
        <li>Lead-gen checklist for Malaysian SMEs</li>
        <li>WhatsApp reply scripts that convert</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <h2>1. What a Malaysian SME website actually costs</h2>
    <p>
      Prices in Malaysia vary wildly — from friends "coding something" for cheap, to agencies quoting five figures.
      The useful breakdown is by what you're actually buying:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>One-page business website</strong> — typically <span class="tag">RM1,500 fixed</span>. Hero, services, contact. Built to look professional and convert. This covers most contractors, clinics, salons, and freelancers.</li>
      <li><strong>Multi-page business website</strong> — RM3,000–5,000 range. Services, team, testimonials, blog, individual product/portfolio pages.</li>
      <li><strong>Web apps &amp; dashboards</strong> — RM5,000+. Ordering systems, customer portals, internal dashboards, automation. Priced per project, never per hour blindly.</li>
      <li><strong>Managed maintenance</strong> — from <span class="tag">RM199/mo</span>. Updates, small edits, uptime, peace of mind.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      A website is a business asset, not a commodity. The cheapest quote is rarely the cheapest once you count
      rework, hidden charges, and a site that doesn't convert.
    </p>

    <div class="quote">
      "A fixed OK quote upfront beats a cheap price plus surprise extras every time."
    </div>

    <h2>2. The fixed-price model (why it's safer for you)</h2>
    <p>
      At HaikaiTech we quote a fixed price before work begins. You know the total, the deliverables, and the timeline
      upfront — no hourly tracking, no surprise invoices. It works like this:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Tell us what you need</strong> — on WhatsApp, with a short description or a screenshot.</li>
      <li><strong>Get a fixed quote</strong> — scope, price, and timeline in writing.</li>
      <li><strong>Pay in milestones</strong> — typically 40% to start, 40% on review, 20% on delivery.</li>
      <li><strong>Launch &amp; maintain</strong> — handover, your domain, optional RM199/mo care.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      You're never locked into a black-box billing model, and both sides know what "done" means.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Lead-gen checklist for Malaysian SMEs</h2>
    <p>Most Malaysian customers reach out on WhatsApp. The businesses that reply fastest (and look professional) win. Use this checklist:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Put a <strong>WhatsApp button above the fold</strong> on your homepage — most visits happen on phones.</li>
      <li>Reply <strong>within the hour during business hours</strong> — speed is a ranking factor for trust.</li>
      <li>Make your <strong>pricing clear</strong> (e.g. a starting price) so the right customers self-qualify.</li>
      <li>Add <strong>testimonials / past work</strong> near your contact CTA.</li>
      <li>Capture emails too — a short "get practical notes" form turns one-time visitors into repeat business.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The single biggest miss for small businesses: owning their list. WhatsApp DMs disappear; an email list (and a
      website you control) keeps working for years.
    </p>

    <h2>4. WhatsApp reply scripts that convert</h2>
    <p>Copy-paste these, then make them your own voice:</p>

    <div class="script"><strong>Fast first reply:</strong> "Hi! Thanks for reaching out — this is Iffat from HaikaiTech. Happy to help. Quick question: are you looking for a brand-new website, or improving one you already have?"</div>
    <div class="script"><strong>Qualify budget/size:</strong> "Got it — that sounds like a solid one-page site (hero, services, contact, WhatsApp button). Our fixed price for that starts at RM1,500 and we'd scope it properly before quoting. Want me to confirm availability this week?"</div>
    <div class="script"><strong>Give a fixed quote:</strong> "Here's the fixed quote: RM2,000 for a one-page site with the sections we discussed, delivered in about 2 weeks. That includes mobile-ready design, WhatsApp button, and handover. No hidden costs — does that work for you?"</div>
    <div class="script"><strong>Follow up without being pushy:</strong> "No stress if you're still deciding! I know you're busy. For reference, most SME sites in your industry take about 2 weeks and start at RM1,500. Happy to answer any questions whenever you're ready."</div>

    <div class="box">
      <h3>Your next step</h3>
      <p>
        Want a fixed quote for your business? Chat on WhatsApp and tell us what you need — we usually reply within the
        hour during business hours (9am–6pm MYT).
      </p>
      <p class="fact">wa.me/60147533499 · hq@haikaitech.my</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta">
      HaikaiTech Solutions · haikaitech.my · SSM 202603149868 (CA0422517-K)<br />
      Fixed-price websites, dashboards &amp; web apps for Malaysian SMEs.
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>